      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/Greater_Manchester/Gorton.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 19th‑century Gorton Monastery, designed by Edward Welby Pugin, is a Grade II* listed example of High Victorian Gothic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/Greater_Manchester/Gorton.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After a 1980s abandonment, the monastery was restored and now hosts weddings, conferences, and other events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/Greater_Manchester/Gorton.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Debdale Park, Manchester’s largest public park, spans more than 45 hectares and is a designated Local Nature Reserve.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/Greater_Manchester/Gorton.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Gorton’s past includes a zoo, an amusement park, an exhibition hall complex, and a speedway stadium.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoverbritainstowns.co.uk/places/gorton/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Gorton’s history of manufacturing and engineering continues to influence the neighbourhood, which remains one of Manchester’s most deprived areas.",
